$$
\alpha_s(p)=
\frac{864D(x_s(p))^3\mathcal S(t_s(p),b_s(p))^2}
 {U(b_s(p))^{23}\mathcal Q(t_s(p),b_s(p))^3}
\mathcal T(t_s(p),b_s(p)).
\tag{30.6}
$$

The multiplier is analytic and nonzero, so it preserves both zeros and
